      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Girl FWD, a program offered by Movemeant, is a group coaching course designed to empower middle and high school girls in today's digital landscape. The program offers three participation options: a virtual platform accessible from anywhere, an in-school curriculum delivered over one semester, and a community-based club model. Girls engage in interactive 30-minute movement sessions, such as dance or kickboxing, followed by guided discussions on relevant topics. Through these activities, participants develop essential life skills, build confidence, and foster resilience. Girl FWD aims to transform both the physical and mental health of young girls while providing a supportive and inclusive environment for learning and growth.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>15020</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Generation Confident is an empowering course by Movemeant for middle school girls, focusing on body acceptance, healthy behaviors, and positive relationships. Led by a dedicated coach, the program covers topics such as body awareness, healthy lifestyle choices, and strategies for dealing with body shaming and bullying. The curriculum, adaptable to various settings like lunchtime or after-school programs, consists of 14 modules taught over one semester or condensed into a ten-week course. Each 40-60 minute session combines thought-provoking discussions with invigorating physical activities like yoga and dance, reinforcing weekly themes. By blending mental and physical nourishment, Generation Confident aims to build strong peer connections and self-trust, promoting a balanced approach to body image and self-esteem in a supportive community.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>14974</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Meant to Move Athletic Grants, a program designed to empower young female athletes from disadvantaged backgrounds, aims to remove barriers to fitness and level the playing field. The program provides $1,000 grants on a rolling basis, offering opportunities for sports instruction, equipment access, athletic coaching, and mentorship. By supporting girls from underserved communities, the program fosters confidence and a lifelong love for sports, helping participants grow mentally, physically, and emotionally. The grants are intended to assist girls in taking their athletic pursuits to the next level, ultimately helping them reach their full potential. Applicants must work with a parent or guardian to complete the application process.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
